=== 10: hash -p refuses a directory
status: 0
bash-n: 0
--- stdout
|[a directory is refused]
|hash: adir: Is a directory
|rc=1
|rc=1
|hash: z1: not found
|rc=1
|[any other path is taken at face value]
|rc=0
|rc=0
|z2	afile
|z3	/nonexistent/x
|rc=0
|[refused once per name]
|hash: adir: Is a directory
|hash: adir: Is a directory
|rc=1
|[a relative path resolves against the shell's working directory]
|hash: reldir: Is a directory
|rc=1
|rc=0
|reldir
|rc=0
|[hash NAME stays strict about executables]
|hash: only: not found
|rc=1
--- dir adir
--- file afile
--- dir d1
--- file d1/only
--- dir sub
--- dir sub/reldir
--- dir sub2

